Z||000008||theogre||08-11-2001||09:43 PM||||Hard to say on the tranny. Over filling usually causes aeration which makes for mushy shifting. (you did check it hot... idling in park... TH125 will read over filled unless it's running.)<P>The TV cable could be out of whack. that could make it shift hard.<P>There are 70+ TSB's on the TH125 tranny. (A bunch for the AOD trannys as well...) A number of them cover shifting problems, nearly all of them are internal problems. Other than checking the TV cable or the governer there's not much you can do for it.<P>There are notes on the TV cable in my cave.<P>The governer is under the VSS drive. it can get crap in it and screw up shifting.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||1
